#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:5
#: bf52ff7aa4c542ca92529cc731f93961
msgid "Autopilot Output Functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:7
#: 1a5c1782f96643beb9770dbba8ae9751
msgid "All autopilot servo/motor outputs may be mapped to any output function supported by ArduPilot. This page describes how to configure these output channels and what each of the available functions that can be assigned to an output are."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:11
#: 2c55d25582b84ed8b12835a031ba46f4
msgid "ArduPilot supports up to 32 outputs. These may be via DroneCAN ESCs or directly from autopilot outputs, or a mixture of both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:13
#: 374f29c1e8234c2d95332439f6aa7cec
msgid "See the left sidebar menu for major output categories to navigate to desired functions on this page quickly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:18
#: f098ebd730fd4798a1a232595565f872
msgid "The SERVOn_FUNCTION parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:20
#: adc3040cdf004e8896b3bc5bf6fd090c
msgid "In the advanced parameter view of your GCS you will find that each SERVO output channel has a ``SERVOn_FUNCTION`` parameter. For example, :ref:`SERVO5_FUNCTION<SERVO5_FUNCTION>`  controls the output function of channel 5, :ref:`SERVO6_FUNCTION<SERVO6_FUNCTION>` controls the output function of channel 6 and so on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:23
#: ec4a03b3578043efa3fed04a6946df9c
msgid "Not all the functions are available in each vehicle. Defaults are set to 0 when firmware for a vehicle type is first loaded. Choosing a frame configuration in Mission Planner during initial setup will set the outputs to the basic typical functions for that frame type. For example, fixed wing plane will set the first four outputs, SERVO1-SERVO4 to Aileron, Elevator, Throttle, and Rudder functions, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:27
#: 6554002b189844e98e3e5aaafe33c0a0
msgid "All of these functions may be used on multiple channels. So if you want 3 elevator channels for some reason you can set ``SERVOn_FUNCTION`` to 19 on 3 of your output channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:32
#: 0bfdaf5825ac4f4ca1c850f0a1431359
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:34
#: d343360ca530420c960819e361593fef
msgid "Configuration can be done using the SERVO tab of Mission Planner or by directly setting the ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` parameter for an output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:39
#: 55b34214ef674b34bad70e33449d3631
msgid "For example, if you wished to re-order a Copter quad-x frame's motors from the :ref:`kitty-corner default <connect-escs-and-motors>` to a more logical clockwise method, make these changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:41
#: d8cf8520ed844f9cbb439c779c409553
msgid ":ref:`SERVO1_FUNCTION <SERVO1_FUNCTION>` leave as 33 (aka \"motor1\", front-right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:42
#: 5dae037fcbed4b559096cbf8e9bcab5e
msgid ":ref:`SERVO2_FUNCTION <SERVO2_FUNCTION>` change from 34 (aka \"motor2\", back-left) to 36 (motor #4, back-right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:43
#: 926e5592dacb45698774d4b2b94d97bf
msgid ":ref:`SERVO3_FUNCTION <SERVO3_FUNCTION>` change from 35 (aka \"motor3\", front-left) to 34 (motor #2, back-left)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:44
#: 439b4dbdfe0b43a78ee08afd647e1a6e
msgid ":ref:`SERVO4_FUNCTION <SERVO4_FUNCTION>` change from 36 (aka \"motor4\", back-right) to 35 (motor #3, front-left)"
msgstr ""

