#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:230
#: 3a71a2fe291d4b24a551718ee6ed739e
msgid "The Aileron output function provides an aileron output, with its own per-channel trim and range. This is useful when you want to trim each aileron separately, or if your main roll control is setup as :ref:`ELEVONS<guide-elevon-plane>`, and you also want some normal ailerons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:239
#: 56baed5f71344692a71ac502adff9afc
msgid "The elevator output function provides an elevator output. Multiple outputs are possible, each with separate per-channel trim and range. This is useful when you want to trim each elevator separately, or if your main pitch control is setup as :ref:`ELEVONS<guide-elevon-plane>`, and you also want some normal elevator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:250
#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:483
#: 4dce0ec844c74c5ea77b9bd0d60b09b2
#: 29200fdb36254a0dba2ea871ae53492b
msgid "Typical servo output for motor power control for vehicles. Multiple outputs can be used for multi-engine vehicles. Primary power control output for normal fixed-wing planes, single rotor helicopter, and rovers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:253
#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:427
#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:486
#: 2dd005e0d656449fa9d62cbe6382f4ba
#: a21183bd419845e18cbb301917bff99a
#: 0d4f7b367b034baf93dab8a7008bd957
msgid "Throttle Left/ Right"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:255
#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:488
#: d35a985a3c474e24961de2c9fa17ff77
#: 49bd41293cce44c1b4ebf981b952c273
msgid "In Plane, these outputs are for differential thrust in twin engine aircraft and the amount of yaw affecting the base throttle value is determined by :ref:`RUDD_DT_GAIN<RUDD_DT_GAIN>`. Also, in Plane's vectored Tailsitters, these are the motor outputs. In Rover, these outputs are for control of the steering motors in :ref:`Skid-Steering Rovers <rover-motor-and-servo-configuration-skid>`. In Copter, these outputs are used for the Bicopter motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:262
#: 513c385243ff4d318dd36237d00aab5d
msgid "The rudder output function provides a rudder outputs with its own per-channel trim and range. Separate rudder channels are particularly useful for nose wheel steering where the nose wheel may need to be reversed as compared to the normal rudder channel or for multi-wheel planes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:271
#: 57c2061e75c543f7b29dcf0f35c3a5e8
msgid "When a channel is set as a flap its value comes from the flap rc input channel selected by assigning ``RCx_FUNCTION`` = 208 to it and/or from the :ref:`Automatic Flaps<automatic-flaps>` feature. The reason you may want to use this instead of a RCPassThru is that you can setup multiple flap channels with different trims and ranges, and you may want to take advantage of the :ref:`FLAP_SLEWRATE<FLAP_SLEWRATE>` to limit the speed of flap movement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:279
#: 76adc03cbddd4e11875e944b4c07239f
msgid "The Automatic Flaps output function behaves like the Flap output, except it can also accept automatic flap output control from the :ref:`TKOFF_FLAP_PCNT<TKOFF_FLAP_PCNT>` and :ref:`LAND_FLAP_PERCNT<LAND_FLAP_PERCNT>` parameters, as well as the :ref:`FLAP_1_SPEED <FLAP_1_SPEED>`, :ref:`FLAP_1_PERCNT<FLAP_1_PERCNT>`, :ref:`FLAP_2_SPEED<FLAP_2_SPEED>` and :ref:`FLAP_2_PERCNT<FLAP_2_PERCNT>` parameters. in addition to manual control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:284
#: 6d60717e34a44b69a19edbc8248f4a41
msgid "If you have both an RC flap input channel set (``RCx_OPTION`` = 208) and the Automatic Flaps function set, then the amount of flap applied is the higher of the two."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:288
#: f93fc1799ec745d3ab0002c3438393b7
msgid "Flaperons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:290
#: 1509773b239c426ab23cdb458a2d49a5
msgid "Using SERVOn_FUNCTION 24 and 25 (FlaperonLeft / FlaperonRight) you can setup flaperons, which are ailerons that double as flaps. They are very useful for aircraft which have ailerons but no flaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:294
#: c030e371262c4bc6a13c7c05c504e874
msgid "See the :ref:`Flaperon guide <flaperons-on-plane>` section for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rcoutput-mapping.rst:296
#: 0c6d950c38ae4537a6dd5b69ba8af2a0
msgid "Note that flaperons act like Automatic or normal flaps, described above for the flap component of the output."
msgstr ""

